    "created_at": "2015-08-24T11:11:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-08-24T11:11:33Z",
    "body": "> Almost everything has changed, hasn't it?\n\nI meant to ask what it was that changed your mind. Maybe just unforseen consequences of the spec changes?\n\nCertainly there are differences between having all nested fullscreen elements in the top layer and having just one, but shouldn't it almost always be the case that the fullscreen element obscures everything else, so that it doesn't matter?\n\nIt seems to me that another possible fix here would be to make the special rendering for the elements in the top layer apply only to the topmost element. In other words, where the spec says \"An element in a top layer has the following characteristics\" it could instead apply those rules only to the topmost element.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
